# sitemap.xml is a generated artifact (npm run sitemap:generate), served
# directly from public/ by an Express route. It used to be committed, which
# meant every deploy's `git checkout -- public/sitemap.xml` (needed to avoid
# pull conflicts from the server's own regenerated copy) silently reset the
# live sitemap back to whatever URL count was last committed — undoing every
# blog-seed deploy that didn't immediately re-run sitemap:generate afterward.
public/sitemap.xml
